PRB-9  CH.PRB- 2.6.
Describe how in a logistic regression model, a transformation to the response variable is
applied to yield a probability distribution. Why is it considered a more informative representation of the response?

Logistic regression is a linear regression followed by a sigmoid function that aims to continuously map input variables to one of two classes. The sigmoid thus serves two purposes: it gives the linear regression flexibility to return any number in the real line, and it squashes the result of the linear regression into 0 and 1, which can be interpreted as the probability of the true class. This can be used to model the likelihood of a class or the posterior probability if the data probability and the prior are known (or modeled). 

